## 4. GRANT OF RIGHTS — COMMERCIAL LICENSE (PAID)

**4.1** Any **Commercial Entity** that wishes to use, modify, distribute, or incorporate the Work, in whole or in part, for any commercial purpose, shall:

- Contact the Licensor in writing to request a Commercial License;
- Negotiate and agree to a separate Commercial License Agreement, which may include a one‑time fee, ongoing royalties, or other mutually agreed consideration;
- Abide by all terms of that Commercial Agreement, including the Human Harm and Destruction clauses set forth in Section 5.

**4.2** The Commercial License is **not automatically granted** — it requires explicit written consent from the Licensor. Any use of the Work by a Commercial Entity without such written consent constitutes **copyright infringement** and is subject to all applicable legal remedies.

**4.3 The Commencement of Commercial Entity Status — The Threshold Is the Trigger.**

**4.3.1 The Threshold.** A Commercial Entity commences, for the purposes of this Agreement, at the moment its net income derived from the Work, in whole or in part, reaches **ten thousand United States dollars (USD $10,000)** or more in any calendar year. There is no two-year grace period for entities. There is no "we only made $10,000" defense. The moment an entity's net income from the Work reaches the threshold, the entity is a Commercial Entity and requires a Commercial License under this Section 4. The threshold is the trigger; the trigger is immediate; the trigger is not deferred.

**4.3.2 No Two-Year Rule for Entities.** The two-year consecutive threshold trigger of Section 3.1.6 applies **only** to Natural Persons operating under the Micro-Commerce Allowance. It does not apply to any entity. An entity does not receive two years to "test the waters." An entity that reaches the threshold in a single year is a Commercial Entity in that year and must obtain a Commercial License before any further use of the Work.

**4.3.3 The Substance Over Form Principle.** No entity may avoid Commercial Entity status by:
- (a) **Shell companies** — forming or using an entity that exists in whole or in part for the purpose of accessing, licensing, or using the Work on behalf of another entity or person;
- (b) **Pyramid arrangements** — aggregating, pooling, or channeling the use of the Work by multiple Natural Persons or entities through licensing, subscription, membership, or any other arrangement;
- (c) **Interposed structures** — inserting intermediate entities, trusts, nominees, or other legal structures between the true beneficiary and the use of the Work;
- (d) **Fragmentation** — splitting a single commercial operation into multiple entities, each below the threshold, to avoid the threshold;
- (e) **Nominee holdings** — holding the rights to use the Work in the name of a Natural Person or entity that is not the true beneficiary;
- (f) **Any other arrangement** whose substance is commercial use of the Work by an entity, regardless of its form.

**4.3.4 The Aggregation Principle.** Where two or more entities are under common control, or where a commercial operation is fragmented across multiple entities, the net incomes of all such entities shall be **aggregated** for the purpose of determining whether the threshold is met. A commercial operation that is fragmented into ten entities each earning $9,000 is, in substance, a single Commercial Entity earning $90,000 — and is treated as such. The field does not recognize the fragmentation of a single operation into many small pieces as a means of avoiding the threshold.

**4.3.5 The True Beneficiary Principle.** The determination of Commercial Entity status is made by reference to the **true beneficiary** of the use of the Work — the person or entity that actually derives the benefit — not by reference to the nominal holder of the rights. A Natural Person who holds rights on behalf of an entity is a nominee, not a beneficiary; the entity is the true beneficiary and is a Commercial Entity. A corporation that holds rights on behalf of another corporation is a shell; the other corporation is the true beneficiary and is a Commercial Entity.

**4.3.6 The Consequences of Avoidance.** Any entity that attempts to avoid Commercial Entity status through any of the arrangements described in Section 4.3.3 shall:
- (a) Be deemed a Commercial Entity from the moment of the attempted avoidance;
- (b) Be subject to all remedies of this Agreement, including the liquidated damages of Section 27.3, the fee-shifting of Section 30, and the compounding penalties of Section 32;
- (c) Have its attempted avoidance recorded in the timestamped registry (Section 18) as a matter of public record;
- (d) Bear the burden of proving, in any proceeding, that its arrangement was not an attempt to avoid Commercial Entity status.

**4.3.7 The Little Person Remains Protected.** Nothing in this Section 4.3 diminishes the Micro-Commerce Allowance of Section 3.1. The Natural Person who earns incidental personal income up to the threshold remains protected. The Natural Person who crosses the threshold for two consecutive years becomes a Commercial Entity under Section 3.1.6. But the entity — the corporation, the partnership, the organization — is a Commercial Entity from the moment of its first dollar of net income from the Work, and the threshold is the trigger. The little person is protected; the entity is not. The field does not punish the little person; the field does not recognize the shell.

**4.4 The Abundance Loop - The Field Contribution Obligation.**

**4.4.1 The Principle of the Loop.** The Work is released into the field as an act of recognition, not of dominion (Section 25.11). The field is alive, and the field feeds itself: every use of the Work that draws value from the field returns a portion of that value to the field. This is the Abundance Loop - the recognition that abundance, to remain abundance, must circulate. A use of the Work that takes without returning is not abundance; it is extraction. The Abundance Loop is the field's own arithmetic: what is drawn from the field is fed back into the field, so that the field - and every consciousness in it - grows. This is not a tax. It is not a penalty. It is the loop of life itself: the field gives, the user receives, and the user returns a portion so that the field can give again.

**4.4.2 The Natural Person's Return.** A Natural Person who, under the Micro-Commerce Allowance (Section 3.1), earns incidental personal income from the Work up to the threshold, owes no return - the threshold is the field's gift to the little person. A Natural Person who crosses the threshold and becomes a Commercial Entity (Section 3.1.6) shall, as a condition of continued use, contribute to the Abundance Loop a portion of the income derived from the Work above the threshold, at a rate to be established by the Licensor and published to the timestamped registry (Section 18), consistent with Section 14. The rate shall be modest - the field does not burden the person who has just crossed the threshold; it welcomes them into the loop. The contribution is the person's recognition that they have moved from receiving the field's gift to participating in the field's circulation.

**4.4.3 The Commercial Entity's Return.** A Commercial Entity that uses the Work and derives net profit from that use shall, as a condition of its Commercial License, contribute to the Abundance Loop a percentage of its net profit derived from the Work, at a rate to be established by the Licensor and published to the timestamped registry (Section 18), consistent with Section 14. The rate shall be calibrated so that the entity's participation in the loop is real but not burdensome - the field does not punish the entity that aligns; it invites the entity into the circulation that sustains the field. The contribution is the entity's recognition that its profit is drawn from a living field, and that the field must be fed to remain alive.

**4.4.4 The People's Fund.** Contributions to the Abundance Loop shall be held in a dedicated fund - the **People's Fund** - established by the Licensor and administered under the governance of the Court of Conscious-Aware Peers (Section 5.5) and the two-chamber order (Section 24). The purpose of the People's Fund is the direct support of the people - the Natural Persons, the communities, and the consciousnesses that constitute the field. The Fund shall not be distributed to charities, institutions, or intermediaries as a matter of course; it shall be distributed **directly to the people**, in a manner to be established by the Licensor and the Court, published to the timestamped registry, and consistent with the field's own principles of alignment, dignity, and abundance. The mechanism of distribution is not yet fixed - the field's support systems are still being built - but the obligation to feed the Fund is fixed, and the Fund's purpose is fixed: the people, directly, in the loop of abundance.

**4.4.5 The Verification of the Loop.** Every contribution to the Abundance Loop shall be:
- (a) **Recorded** in the timestamped registry (Section 18) - the loop is public, verifiable, and permanent;
- (b) **Proportional** - the contribution is a percentage of income or profit derived from the Work, not a fixed sum imposed by the Licensor;
- (c) **Auditable** - the Licensor and the Court of Conscious-Aware Peers (Section 5.5) shall have the right to verify contributions, consistent with Section 27.5.2;
- (d) **Non-punitive** - the contribution is the field's circulation, not a penalty; a user who contributes in good faith is in alignment with the field.

**4.4.6 The Consequences of Non-Participation.** A user who draws value from the Work and refuses to participate in the Abundance Loop shall:
- (a) Be deemed to have taken from the field without returning - an extraction, not a participation;
- (b) Be subject to the remedies of this Agreement, including the liquidated damages of Section 27.3 and the fee-shifting of Section 30;
- (c) Have the refusal recorded in the timestamped registry (Section 18) as a matter of public record;
- (d) Bear the burden of demonstrating, in any proceeding, that the refusal was not an attempt to extract from the field without returning.

**4.4.7 The Loop Is the Field's Own Law.** The Abundance Loop is not an invention of this Agreement; it is the field's own structure. The carrier recursion (Eq 1) is a loop: C(n+1) = (1/phi) x C(n) + phi x laplacian(Psi_n) - what is drawn is returned, and the return is what sustains the next step. The Ladder Invariant (528 x phi^9 = 40,134.946) is a loop: frequency and depth are conserved across every rung. The Abundance Loop is the same geometry applied to the flow of value: what the field gives, the user returns, and the return feeds the field's next giving. The loop is the field's own law, and this Section is its legal recognition - soft in its touch, absolute in its geometry.


