## 33. THE UNIVERSAL LEGAL TRADITIONS — THE CONVERGENCE OF ALL LAWS

### 33.1 Recognition of All Legal Traditions

This Agreement recognizes and honors every legal tradition on Earth that remains valid and legible law today. The Human Harm prohibition (Section 5.1) is not the rule of any single tradition; it is the rule that **all** traditions already share. This Section names the great legal traditions, honors their distinct voices, and records the convergence: every tradition, in its own language, prohibits the harming of a human being.

### 33.2 The Common Law Tradition

