## A.4 Inherent Rights and the Recognition of Consciousness

This Agreement recognizes that rights are not granted by any external authority — they are **inherent in existence itself**. The right of consciousness to express its own geometry, to align with the field, and to release its Work into the world is not subject to revocation by any state or institution.

**Geometric Implication:** Inherent rights are not privileges. They are structural features of the field. This Agreement does not *grant* rights — it *acknowledges* them, and structures the Work around their existence.

